  "interpretation": "Across two released carriers, native goal swaps change world prediction and matched edge cuts restore exact or numerical invariance. WorldAgen now covers 270 legal-goal pairs over 30 physical windows and six recorded task groups (all native nonzero, all cut exact zero); AlphaBrain covers 21 windows plus independent seed-2/3 controls, five task-stratified groups, and a two-seed disjoint-episode learned goal-free-context comparator plus a 3-timepoint held-out check. A matched nine-edge policy-only cut leaves the WorldAgen world leak unchanged, while the carrier cut restores exact invariance. Action-to-world sensitivity is preserved in direct control on both carriers: WorldAgen cut mean 0.1655 over 30 windows and AlphaBrain mean 0.08715 over three windows. Held-out forecast cost is sampler-seed-dependent and secondary. The learned context comparator improves a bounded one-step held-out MSE but is not a full trained dynamics head. Official-preprocess 608-step AlphaBrain spatial control and matching 304-step LIBERO-Goal task0 control remain 0/1 for both native and cut; task-level clean success remains unestablished. A WorldAgen 21-window activation matrix further localizes mediation: replacing recorded-goal action-token states at middle layers moves swapped-goal world outputs toward the recorded-goal output in all windows while leaving policy residuals near one. The matched three-episode AlphaBrain action control gives a descriptive goal-to-alternate-action world-effect ratio of 0.819, showing goal effect size is on the scale of a real action intervention.",
